  "worked_solution": "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(-x)+2,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Reflect it across the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(-x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234522/assets/1b60eeb882c85423bb0550c2b6def0d073d53747479bf322976db313ffdf4109.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, translate the result  up by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=f(-x)+2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234522/assets/58a681bf9aa47521b30761e904dad8e816e2077387c28b132d2480bb39ea4baa.png)",
